{"ticker":"WAB","updated":"2026-10-30T23:22:46Z","profile":{"longName":"Westinghouse Air Brake Technologies Corporation","shortName":"Westinghouse Air Brake Technolo","sector":"Industrials","industry":"Railroads","country":"United States","website":"https://www.wabteccorp.com","fullTimeEmployees":31000,"marketCap":47227473920,"trailingPE":34.732918,"forwardPE":22.224695,"priceToSalesTrailing12Months":3.8666673,"pegRatio":1.37,"targetMeanPrice":332.08334,"targetHighPrice":355.0,"targetLowPrice":292.0,"numberOfAnalystOpinions":12,"recommendationKey":"strong_buy","revenueGrowth":0.081,"earningsGrowth":0.337,"grossMargins":0.36172,"operatingMargins":0.20224,"profitMargins":0.111999996,"totalRevenue":12213999616,"beta":0.917,"fiftyTwoWeekHigh":306.64,"fiftyTwoWeekLow":194.93,"currency":"USD","exchange":"NYQ","quoteType":"EQUITY","dividendYield":0.43},"summary":"Westinghouse Air Brake Technologies Corporation provides locomotives, equipment, systems, and services for the freight rail and passenger transit industries worldwide. It operates in two segments, Freight and Transit. It offers diesel-electric and liquid natural gas-powered locomotives; engines, electric motors, and propulsion systems; and marine and mining products. The company also offers positive train control equipment; electronically controlled pneumatic braking products; railway electronics; signal design and engineering services; distributed locomotive power, and train cruise and remote controls; industrial/mobile Internet of Things hardware and software, edge-to-cloud, on and off-board analytics and rules, and asset performance management solutions; rail and shipper transportation management, and port visibility and optimization solutions; and network optimization solutions. In addition, it provides freight car trucks, braking equipment, and related components; air compressors and dryers, as well as heating, ventilation, and air conditioning (HVAC) systems; heat transfer components and systems; custom engi